# REQUIRES: python-api, jax
# The JAX adapter of the frame evaluator, mdir.jax (D371,
# docs/python-frames.md, The JAX adapter), on the CPU, in double and mixed
# precision, Inputs/python_frames_jax.py: the energies, the gradient in the
# positions, and the Jacobian in the tunables against
# FrameEvaluator.evaluate, and vmap against a loop and jit against eager, to
# the bit; in double precision, central differences of the energy in
# params, the positions, and the cell, and jax.test_util.check_grads; every
# row of the refusal matrix, the errors of data, and the dtype table; the
# second pass, jacobian="recompute" (D375),
# against the kept Jacobian to 1e-12, with its central differences, its
# cost in evaluations, and its refusals.
# JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu keeps a JAX with a CUDA plugin on the CPU, where the
# target is registered.
# RUN: env JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide gate Double CPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=GATE,FD -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: env JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide gate Mixed CPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=GATE -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# RUN: env JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide refusals Double CPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=REFUSE,REFUSE-DOUBLE -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: env JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide refusals Mixed CPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=REFUSE,REFUSE-MIXED -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# RUN: env JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide second Double CPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=SECOND,SECOND-FD -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: env JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide second Mixed CPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=SECOND -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# GATE: [[MODE]]: the energies, the gradient in the positions, and the Jacobian in the tunables against FrameEvaluator.evaluate, to the bit: True
# GATE: [[MODE]]: one frame, eager and under jit, to the bit: True
# GATE: [[MODE]]: the energy's gradients in params, the positions, and the cell of each frame, vmap and jit(vmap) against a loop, jit against eager, to the bit: True
# GATE: [[MODE]]: nested vmap, frames on the second axis, and one cell for every frame against a loop, to the bit: True
# FD: [[MODE]]: central differences in params['sigma']: largest relative error
# FD: [[MODE]]: central differences in params['q']: largest relative error
# FD: [[MODE]]: central differences in the positions: largest relative error
# FD: [[MODE]]: central differences in the edges of the cell: largest relative error
# FD: [[MODE]]: central differences in the six numbers of a triclinic cell (3, 3): largest relative error
# FD: [[MODE]]: jax.test_util.check_grads(order=1, modes=('fwd', 'rev')) in params, step 1e-07: passed
# FD: [[MODE]]: jax.test_util.check_grads(order=1, modes=('fwd', 'rev')) in the positions, step 1e-07: passed
# FD: [[MODE]]: jax.test_util.check_grads(order=1, modes=('fwd', 'rev')) in the edges, step 3e-05: passed
# FD: [[MODE]]: jax.test_util.check_grads(order=1, modes=('fwd', 'rev')) in the six numbers of a triclinic cell (3, 3), step 3e-05: passed
# GATE: jax passed
# REFUSE: [[MODE]]: refused at trace time: every second derivative (9 forms, under jit too), vmap over params, jax_enable_x64 off, a missing or an extra name of params, a wrong shape or type of params, the positions, or the cell
# REFUSE: [[MODE]]: a derivative in params whose Jacobian passes jacobian_bytes is refused, for one frame and for the frames of a vmap; the gradient in the positions is given
# REFUSE: [[MODE]]: the gradient in the cell of a program with restraints to reference positions is refused; the gradient in the positions is given
# REFUSE: [[MODE]]: a position that is not finite and a cell below twice the cutoff raise an error of JAX naming the frame of the call, eager and under jit; the function then gives the same energy, to the bit
# REFUSE: [[MODE]]: eval_shape, lax.scan, jax.checkpoint, a cell (3, 3) whose gradient has the edges on its diagonal, and the program's cell: True
# REFUSE: [[MODE]]: a compiled call names the program by its key and its fingerprint; a key that was released is refused when the executable is instantiated
# REFUSE-DOUBLE: [[MODE]]: float32 positions are refused; float64 give a float64 gradient: True
# REFUSE-MIXED: [[MODE]]: deterministic: float32 positions refused; not deterministic (forces in f32): float32 positions give the f32 forces of the program and float64 positions those forces widened, to the bit: True
# REFUSE: jax passed
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, grad of a weighted sum over a vmap:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, the same under jit:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, value_and_grad in params, the positions, and the cell:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, jvp in params of the batch:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, jax.linearize in params, applied:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, jacfwd in params:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, jacrev in params:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, vmap of grad:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, grad of one frame, eager and under jit:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the second pass against the kept Jacobian, jvp of one frame under jit:
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: the frames evaluated for a derivative in params of 4 frames, with the Jacobian kept and with the second pass: grad 4 and 4, value_and_grad 4 and 8
# SECOND: [[MODE]]: refused: an unknown jacobian, every second derivative through the second pass, vmap over params; above jacobian_bytes, jacobian='keep' names the second pass, which jacobian_bytes does not bound: True
# SECOND-FD: [[MODE]]: the second pass, central differences in params['sigma']: relative error
# SECOND-FD: [[MODE]]: the second pass, central differences in params['q']: relative error
# SECOND-FD: [[MODE]]: the second pass, jax.test_util.check_grads(order=1, modes=('fwd', 'rev')) in params, step 1e-07: passed
# SECOND: jax passed
